--
N5008 [temp.deduct.call]/4.3 + [over.match.funcs]: header-free, cvise-reduced
model of the libstdc++ std::get<0> write path (std::get -> std::__get_helper ->
_Tuple_impl::_M_head, with _M_head inherited from _Head_base); returns 42 under
a conforming compiler (verified with g++).

get<0>'s constexpr body now converts: __get_helper<0> resolves the inherited
static _M_head call by a derived-to-base conversion of the by-value argument
even with the sibling SFINAE __get_helper overload present, so the write
through std::get<0>'s reference takes effect.  Non-vacuous: assertion 1 (write
took effect) SUCCEEDs and assertion 2 (a wrong value) FAILs.
